(Cross-posting from https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/139610#issuecomment-2791500044)

The way to name the *real* never type on stable Rust is:

```rust
mod fn_ret {
    pub trait FnRet {
        type Output;
    }

    impl<R> FnRet for fn() -> R {
        type Output = R;
    }
}

pub type Never = <fn() -> ! as fn_ret::FnRet>::Output;
```

(The [`never-say-never` crate](https://crates.io/crates/never-say-never), with nearly 1.5 million downloads, uses this trick.)
